<div class="mb-8">
  <Heading size="2xl" as="h1" class="mb-2">Accordion</Heading>
  <Text size=lg tone="subdued" as="h2">
    A vertically stacked set of collapsible content sections, useful for organizing related information
    into digestible chunks without overwhelming the page.
  </Text>
</div>

<!-- Canonical example -->
<div class="mb-8">
  <Example align="start" source={'
    <Accordion>
      <Accordion:Item value="item-1">
        <Item:Trigger><Icon name="accessibility"/>Is it accessible?</Item:Trigger>
        Yes. It adheres to the WAI-ARIA design pattern.
      </Accordion:Item>
      <Accordion:Item value="item-2">
        <Item:Trigger><Icon name="paintbrush"/>Is it styled?</Item:Trigger>
        Yes. It ships with default styles using Tailwind CSS.
      </Accordion:Item>
      <Accordion:Item value="item-3">
        <Item:Trigger><Icon name="clapperboard" />Is it animated?</Item:Trigger>
        Yes. It uses CSS transitions for smooth expand and collapse.
      </Accordion:Item>
    </Accordion>
  '}/>
</div>

<!-- Usage -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Usage</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <CodeBlock code={"<Accordion>\n  <Accordion:Item value=\"unique-key\">\n    <Item:Trigger>Section title</Item:Trigger>\n    Section content goes here.\n  </Accordion:Item>\n</Accordion>"}/>
  </div>
  <Prose class="mt-4">
    <p>
      The component uses a nested slot structure. Each item requires a unique
      <code>value</code> prop that identifies it within the accordion.
    </p>
  </Prose>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-muted/50 overflow-hidden mt-4">
    <CodeBlock code={"Accordion\n├── Accordion:Item\n│   ├── Item:Trigger\n│   └── (default content)\n└── Accordion:Item\n    ├── Item:Trigger\n    └── (default content)"}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- When to Use -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">When to Use</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Accordions work best when users need to scan multiple sections and selectively dive into one or
      two at a time. Common use cases include FAQ pages, settings panels, and filter groups in sidebars.
    </p>
    <p>
      Avoid accordions when the content is short enough to display all at once, or when users are
      likely to need all sections open simultaneously. In those cases, plain headings with visible
      content will reduce clicks and cognitive load.
    </p>
    <p>
      For just two options that toggle between each other, consider a
      <a href="/components/tabs">Tabs</a> component instead.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Behaviour -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Behaviour</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Multiple sections can be open at the same time. Opening one section does not close others,
      letting users compare content across sections side by side.
    </p>
    <p>
      Expanding and collapsing is animated with a smooth height transition. The chevron icon rotates
      to indicate the current state of each section.
    </p>
    <p>
      The entire trigger row is clickable, not just the text. This provides a generous hit target,
      especially on touch devices.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Examples -->
<div class="flex flex-col gap-12 mb-12">
  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Default Expanded</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>
        Use the <code>expanded</code> attribute to pre-open a section on page load. This is useful
        when the first section contains the most relevant information, or when you want to hint at the
        kind of content hidden in the other sections.
      </p>
    </Prose>
    <Example align="start" source={'
      <Accordion>
        <Accordion:Item value="open" expanded>
          <Item:Trigger>This section starts open</Item:Trigger>
          Content is visible immediately without user interaction.
        </Accordion:Item>
        <Accordion:Item value="closed">
          <Item:Trigger>This section starts closed</Item:Trigger>
          Click to reveal this content.
        </Accordion:Item>
      </Accordion>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">With Icons</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>
        Place an icon inside the trigger slot to give each section a visual anchor. Icons help users
        scan the list faster and find the section they need without reading every label.
      </p>
    </Prose>
    <Example align="start" source={'
      <Accordion>
        <Accordion:Item value="profile">
          <Item:Trigger><Icon name="user"/>Profile</Item:Trigger>
          Manage your name, avatar, and personal details.
        </Accordion:Item>
        <Accordion:Item value="notifications">
          <Item:Trigger><Icon name="bell"/>Notifications</Item:Trigger>
          Choose which events trigger email or push notifications.
        </Accordion:Item>
        <Accordion:Item value="security">
          <Item:Trigger><Icon name="lock"/>Security</Item:Trigger>
          Update your password and configure two-factor authentication.
        </Accordion:Item>
      </Accordion>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Rich Content</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>
        Accordion content is not limited to plain text. You can nest any components inside the
        body, including form fields, lists, or other interactive elements.
      </p>
    </Prose>
    <Example align="start" source={'
      <Accordion>
        <Accordion:Item value="shipping" expanded>
          <Item:Trigger><Icon name="truck"/>Shipping Information</Item:Trigger>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <TextField name="address" label="Street address" fullwidth/>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
              <TextField name="city" label="City" fullwidth/>
              <TextField name="zip" label="ZIP code" fullwidth/>
            </div>
          </div>
        </Accordion:Item>
        <Accordion:Item value="billing">
          <Item:Trigger><Icon name="credit-card"/>Billing Details</Item:Trigger>
          <Text tone="subdued">Enter your payment information here.</Text>
        </Accordion:Item>
      </Accordion>
    '}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Best Practices -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Best Practices</Heading>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-green-500/30 bg-green-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-green-600">Do</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Keep trigger labels short and descriptive.</li>
          <li>Use consistent naming patterns across sections.</li>
          <li>Pre-expand the most important section when the page loads.</li>
          <li>Group related items under a single accordion rather than scattering them.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-red-600">Don't</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Nest accordions inside other accordions.</li>
          <li>Hide critical information that users must see to complete a task.</li>
          <li>Use an accordion for a single item — just show the content directly.</li>
          <li>Put entire page sections inside an accordion; use page navigation instead.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- API Reference -->
<div>
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">API Reference</Heading>

  <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 mt-6">Accordion</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Prop</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Type</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Values</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Default</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground" colspan="4">No props — accepts Accordion:Item children via slots.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 mt-6">Accordion:Item</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Prop</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Type</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Values</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Default</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y">
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">value</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any unique string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">required</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">expanded</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Boolean</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true, false</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">false</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 mt-6">Item:Trigger</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Slot</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">Item:Trigger</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">The clickable header content. Accepts text, icons, or any inline elements.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
